16c4AtUiX","name":"Bug","description":"An unexpected problem or behavior","color":"red","created_at":"2024-02-04T06:23:35Z","updated_at":"2024-07-26T13:08:28Z","is_enabled":true},"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Bug Decription\n\nThis issue tracks the fix for the accepted private security report GHSA-363g-p2fj-3559.\n\nThe report concerns PFCP association overwrite when an unauthorized peer with N4 access sends an Association Setup Request claiming an existing SMF Node ID, causing loss of existing downlink forwarding and enabling subsequent GTP-U traffic redirection.\n\n## To Reproduce\n\nThe reproduction steps, technical analysis, and supporting evidence are available in the private advisory:\n\nhttps://github.com/free5gc/free5gc/security/advisories/GHSA-363g-p2fj-3559\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nThe N4/PFCP trust boundary should prevent unauthorized peers from replacing an established SMF association and taking control of the associated forwarding state.\n\n## Environment\n\n- free5GC Version: v4.2.2","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/free5gc/issues/1224/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/free5gc/issues/1224/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}